{"name":"Eternal Darkness","hex":"#1c2841","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"eternal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Lasting forever; unending.","Existing outside time; as opposed to sempiternal, existing within time but everlastingly."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One who lives forever; an immortal."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eternal"},{"term":"darkness","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The state of being dark; lack of light; the absolute or comparative absence of light.","The state or quality of reflecting little light, of tending to a blackish or brownish color."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/darkness"}],"entries":[{"title":"Eternal Darkness","blocks":[{"text":"Eternal Darkness: Sanity's Requiem is a 2002 horror game developed by Silicon Knights and published by Nintendo for the GameCube. It was produced and directed by Denis Dyack. The game follows the story of several characters across a period of two millennia and four different locations on Earth, as they contend with an ancient evil who seeks to enslave humanity. The gameplay distinguishes itself with unique \"sanity effects\", visual and audial effects that confuse the player and often break the fourth wall."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/8d/Eternal_Darkness_box.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eternal_Darkness","wikidata":"Q1258080"},{"title":"Eternal Darkness (EP)","blocks":[{"text":"Eternal Darkness is the debut EP of Battery, released in 1991 by COP International."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/29/Battery_-_Eternal_Darkness.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eternal_Darkness_(EP)","wikidata":"Q104853128"},{"title":"Darkness","blocks":[{"text":"Darkness is the condition resulting from a lack of illumination, or an absence of visible light."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Creation_of_Light.png/330px-Creation_of_Light.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Darkness","wikidata":"Q204170"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/cb/EternalDarknessSpellCrafting.jpg/330px-EternalDarknessSpellCrafting.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/cb/EternalDarknessSpellCrafting.jpg/330px-EternalDarknessSpellCrafting.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The crafting menu allows the player to experiment and discover new spells.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEternalDarknessSpellCrafting.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Denis_Dyack_in_E3_2003.jpg/500px-Denis_Dyack_in_E3_2003.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Denis_Dyack_in_E3_2003.jpg/1280px-Denis_Dyack_in_E3_2003.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Denis_Dyack_in_E3_2003.jpg/500px-Denis_Dyack_in_E3_2003.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Director and producer Denis Dyack in 2003","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADenis_Dyack_in_E3_2003.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/The_Calling_of_Saint_Matthew-Caravaggo_%281599-1600%29.jpg/500px-The_Calling_of_Saint_Matthew-Caravaggo_%281599-1600%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/The_Calling_of_Saint_Matthew-Caravaggo_%281599-1600%29.jpg/1280px-T